 {"id":"TJ-DF-044","title":"[P1] Landlock TCP egress tier (TJ-GAP-083) silently inert through the INSTALLED CLI: install.sh never ships standalone/landlock-net-loader.py, and the wrapper swallows the engine's loud degrade warning","status":"pending","priority":"P1","created_at":"2026-10-13T17:01:57+00:00","updated_at":"2026-10-13T17:01:57+00:00","reasoning":"Dogfood 2026-10-13 (15th run, first drive of the Landlock fs+net tiers, shipped 2026-10-07 in the unreleased 1.3.0). REPRO (fresh clone of HEAD 4691ac7 into /tmp, ./install.sh, TERMINAL_JAIL_LANDLOCK_NET=1): (a) repo-checkout wrapper standalone/terminal-jail ENFORCES the tier — payload connect() to a live non-allowlisted listener on 127.0.0.1:9151 returns EPERM with the 'kernel egress tier APPLIED' banner; (b) the INSTALLED wrapper ~/.local/bin/terminal-jail does NOT enforce — same probe returns CONNECT-OK (rc 0), i.e. the operator who enabled the documented opt-in tier gets zero containment through the installed CLI. TWO causes, both need fixing: (1) install.sh copies seccomp-loader.py and landlock-loader.py to ~/.local/lib/terminal-jail/ (install.sh:1219-1227) but has NO landlock-net-loader.py copy; the bridge resolved from the INSTALLED plugin tree then walks for the loader next to the plugin and degrades: 'landlock-net-loader.py not found next to the plugin'. (2) The degrade warning is emitted by the bridge on stderr, and the wrapper's _interruptor_evaluate discards bridge stderr (standalone/terminal-jail:271 'python3 \"$bridge\" 2>/dev/null') — the tier silently disappears. Verified end-to-end twice (with and without a live listener; ECONNREFUSED control arm shows the tier-off verdict reads as a normal refusal). Fix direction: install the net loader alongside the fs loader AND surface bridge-stderr warnings on the wrapper's stderr (or re-emit the tier-status line itself).","evidence":[{"probe":"TERMINAL_JAIL_LANDLOCK_NET=1 ~/.local/bin/terminal-jail python3 -c '<connect 127.0.0.1:9151>' -> CONNECT-OK (installed) vs EPERM (checkout wrapper)","description":"[P1] Landlock TCP egress tier (TJ-GAP-083) silently inert through the INSTALLED CLI: install.sh never ships standalone/landlock-net-loader.py, and the wrapper swallows the engine's loud degrade warning"}],"created_by":"terminal-jail-dogfood","description":"Dogfood 2026-10-13 (15th run, first drive of the Landlock fs+net tiers, shipped 2026-10-07 in the unreleased 1.3.0). REPRO (fresh clone of HEAD 4691ac7 into /tmp, ./install.sh, TERMINAL_JAIL_LANDLOCK_NET=1): (a) repo-checkout wrapper standalone/terminal-jail ENFORCES the tier — payload connect() to a live non-allowlisted listener on 127.0.0.1:9151 returns EPERM with the 'kernel egress tier APPLIED' banner; (b) the INSTALLED wrapper ~/.local/bin/terminal-jail does NOT enforce — same probe returns CONNECT-OK (rc 0), i.e. the operator who enabled the documented opt-in tier gets zero containment through the installed CLI. TWO causes, both need fixing: (1) install.sh copies seccomp-loader.py and landlock-loader.py to ~/.local/lib/terminal-jail/ (install.sh:1219-1227) but has NO landlock-net-loader.py copy; the bridge resolved from the INSTALLED plugin tree then walks for the loader next to the plugin and degrades: 'landlock-net-loader.py not found next to the plugin'. (2) The degrade warning is emitted by the bridge on stderr, and the wrapper's _interruptor_evaluate discards bridge stderr (standalone/terminal-jail:271 'python3 \"$bridge\" 2>/dev/null') — the tier silently disappears. Verified end-to-end twice (with and without a live listener; ECONNREFUSED control arm shows the tier-off verdict reads as a normal refusal). Fix direction: install the net loader alongside the fs loader AND surface bridge-stderr warnings on the wrapper's stderr (or re-emit the tier-status line itself)."}
